  "goodToKnow": "Die Photovoltaik (PV, also spelled Fotovoltaik) is photovoltaics, generating electricity from sunlight with Solarmodule. Germany pioneered it through the 2000 renewable energy law (EEG) with guaranteed feed-in tariffs. Balkonkraftwerke, small plug-in solar panels for balconies, have become hugely popular, and rules were simplified in 2024. Solarthermie produces heat instead. It has no plural."
